89:Completed features must have durable evaluator evidence. From the evaluator-evidence baseline onward, `status=done` and `passes=true` are valid only when a run record contains `EVAL_PASS: Fxxx` for that feature. This prevents verification commands alone from being mistaken for evaluator-gated completion.
117:Goal: add an A/B-testable fast work entrypoint that avoids an extra Coding Agent child process while preserving mandatory cold-start Evaluator Agent isolation and evaluator-gated completion.
309:Included scope: record human evaluation outcomes and feedback in durable run artifacts; keep machine Evaluator completion independent from human acceptance timing; reopen the original Feature when human feedback says its original acceptance criteria are not met; preserve attempts and history while allowing a human-reopened Feature to be selected again after it was blocked by an automatic retry limit; support batch evaluation over multiple completed Features; and classify feedback as either unmet current Feature scope or an independent new requirement before any new Feature is planned.
317:Ambiguities or assumptions: the human or coordinating agent is responsible for deciding whether feedback contradicts the original acceptance criteria or requests independent new value; the harness records that decision but does not infer it from prose; a human pass is advisory product acceptance and does not replace the Evaluator Agent evidence required for machine completion; a batch may contain mixed outcomes and mixed classifications; a batch record is evidence and planning input, not a feature generator.
337:Constraints: the adapter contract remains vendor-neutral and commands continue to run without a shell; `cwd` has one documented resolution base and is shared by preflight and real execution; prompt rendering has one layout source of truth rather than hand-maintained per-provider path guesses; hidden-layout legacy root files must remain unchanged during regression tests; generated and upgraded projects must receive the contract without overwriting project-owned state or merge-sensitive root recovery files; and feature completion still requires separate Evaluator evidence.
377:Core flows: an agent reads the installed skill and learns that automatic Evaluator completion may proceed without waiting for Human Eval; an operator records `make human-eval` or `make human-eval-batch`; current-scope feedback returns to the original Feature; independent new value becomes a Planning Agent input; and the run record plus `human_acceptance` metadata preserve the evidence chain.
466:Goal: make a completed Feature mean that one identified attempt, with unchanged acceptance criteria and an identified uncommitted-capable code snapshot, passed program-recorded verification and independent evaluation. Detect accidental drift and refuse completion while preserving the working tree for recovery.
468:Scope included: structured run manifests and receipts; deterministic code/criteria fingerprints; one completion gate for baseline and work-fast; mandatory command execution evidence; dependency-aware scheduling; protected lifecycle state and consistent human reopen handling; single-writer atomic state updates; post-role change guards; visible/hidden install and upgrade distribution with compatible historical evidence.
475:3. The orchestrator checks run/Feature/criteria identity, required checks, evaluator result, state invariants and unchanged source before saving a receipt then setting done through a shared gate. Invalid, missing, stale or contradictory evidence must fail closed with attributable recovery records and a non-success execution result.
476:4. A later Feature may change the repository without invalidating historical completion receipts. Reopening a Feature creates a new run; old coding/evaluation evidence cannot satisfy it. Human acceptance history survives.
479:Constraints: standard-library Python plus real Git; no new service. Harness-generated IDs/fingerprints/command results must not be trusted merely because an agent wrote JSON. Capture evaluator output from its actual child invocation; persist receipts under runs with strict schema and explicit source. Receipts are an accidental-error integrity boundary, not a security boundary against arbitrary filesystem writes. Preserve user provider choice, working tree, unknown state fields, Feature ordering, attempts/history, root project recovery entrypoints, and installed project-owned files. work-fast and work must use the same completion policy. No commits during coding/evaluation.
484:- The harness itself changes during this rollout. F045 delivers independently testable primitives; F046 enrolls all newly started real runs in receipt enforcement. Preserve already completed legacy Features without fabricated new receipts; identify legacy evidence explicitly, freeze any compatibility list instead of granting a global feature-number bypass, and ensure fresh installs enforce receipts from F001. Historical inconsistent metadata (notably F043 done plus reopen_pending) must be visibly diagnosed, never silently rewritten or treated as valid evidence for a new run; new enrolled transitions must be strictly consistent.
486:- Required verification always includes the project recovery command; additional Feature-specific argv checks are optional declarations fixed at run start. Avoid recursive init/test execution in fixtures and circular receipt checks before the candidate Feature is done. Record tests performed by the runner separately from an evaluator's assertions.
495:Decomposition: F045 is the reusable receipt/snapshot capability with one deterministic data validation surface. F046 independently integrates it into actual completion and migration behavior. F047 owns dependency and lifecycle transaction invariants. F048 owns role-boundary detection and recovery, which needs established run identities and state transactions. Documentation, regression tests and bundled copies stay with their owning Feature. The final distribution advances the template version consistently so installed projects can obtain the changes through upgrade.

